            <ArticleTitle>The posterior triangle and the painful shoulder: spinal accessory nerve injury.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>521-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Forty-three cases of accessory nerve injury referred to the Peripheral Nerve Injury Unit have been reviewed. Accessory nerve injury results in a characteristic group of symptoms and signs. Referral for treatment is usually delayed, the average time being 11.3 months. Surgical treatment resulted in improvement of symptoms in almost all cases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
